  "provenance": {
    "kind": "profile",
    "note": "12 tracked 7i shots on hd_golf, fundamentals. Ten are not mishits, so the typical shot is the median of an even count (call 4): the ten carries' middle two are 150 and 150, and the ten start-line offlines' middle two are both 0.0, by stats::percentile's interpolation. The window is 0.1 x 150 = 15.0 yd, exactly. 165.0 sits on the edge and is consistent (inclusive); 165.1 is not; 120.0 is the carry outlier; launch direction 6.0 at 151 yd starts 15.78 yd right, the offline outlier. One shot is a confirmed mishit (manual_mishit) inside both windows, carry 149 and straight, and is a miss (decision 6); one is an automatic mishit at 92 yd. Neither mishit enters the median. No shape is declared, so the shapes are absent; hd_golf prints no impact offset and no low point. Working. 7i consistency: 12 judged; typical carry 150.0 yd and start-line offline 0.0 yd, the medians of the 10 non-mishit judged shots; window 15.0 yd; consistent 7, missed 2026-09-02/2 (carry 165.1, offline 0.000), 2026-09-02/3 (carry 120.0, offline 0.000), 2026-09-02/4 (carry 151.0, offline 15.784), 2026-09-02/5 (mishit, carry 149.0), 2026-09-02/6 (mishit, carry 92.0). 7i consistency grade 7/12 = 0.5833333333333334, Wilson [0.3195, 0.8067]. 7i blend 0.5833333333333334, averaging ['consistency'] and excluding []. player consistency: pooled over 7i, 12 judged, grade 7/12 = 0.5833333333333334, Wilson [0.3195, 0.8067]. player blend 0.5833333333333334, averaging ['consistency'] and excluding []. 7i list: scatter on ball_speed_mph at 2.6772; scatter on carry_distance_yds at 2.4603; strength on start_line_offline_yds at 0.8850. player list: empty, nothing established either way.",
    "oracle": "hand",
    "source": "worked by hand in M37 P5, against the M37 plan's decisions 1-8 and calls 2-12 and its P1-P4 findings, before P6-P9 build the code that must meet it. The grades, shares, Wilson intervals (z = 1.959963984540054, each bound clamped to the share and to [0, 1]), the medians, the grid, heel/toe's counts, the blends and the list's kinds, order and ratios are the hand's. Three kinds of number are carried rather than worked, each from the Rust function the plan says P6-P9 read it from, and gated elsewhere: strike.ball_speed and strike.dispersion, and the dispersion each list is ranked from, are analysis::club_profile::build_bag_profile's per club and analysis::dispersion::build_dispersion's over the whole corpus for the player (the career family gates both); heel/toe's mean_offset_mm and its interval are analysis::stats' mean_and_sd and mean_ci over the listed offsets. The corpus is hand-built as crates/storage::read_corpus writes one: each shot a whole ShotData, each launch_monitor row shot_measure's over the analysed view, and each flight or pose row a hand stand-in (detail 'hand'). The rules as worked: a club's topic exists when its every input is printed on one of the club's shots (capability::printed_on), low point only for an iron, wedge or hybrid, and a shape only when one of the club's shots declared it (call 7); its judged shots count toward metrics, are not shot_needs_review, and hold the inputs in the analysed view, and one whose input is printed on it and blank is unscored under its shot_unscored reason, else printed_blank (call 8); the player pools each topic over the clubs it exists for, and over the untagged shots for strike location and the shapes (call 9); a blend is the left-to-right sum of its graded shares in topic order over their count (call 11). The list (call 12) reads each club's ClubProfile.dispersion, and for the player the whole corpus' kept to club-independent metrics, over launch_monitor rows only: a weakness is an established bias, ratio |offset| / tolerance, or scatter, ratio sd / tolerance, largest first, ties in METRIC_TARGETS order and bias before scatter; a strength is a metric with a target whose center_ci lies inside target +/- tolerance (inclusive) and whose sd_ci.high is below the tolerance (strict), ratio max(|center_ci end - target|, sd_ci.high) / tolerance, smallest first, after every weakness"
  }
